      "sha": "e43c7e965cdf25552ffa40b4512989a998f3d9b1"
     }
    ],
    "commit": {
     "message": "Fix ambiguous hard-suite cases\n\nTwo Ukrainian language items had a second normative answer (СУМ gives both «хворіти на що» and «чим»; «завжди» has a variant stress). They are replaced by two Dutch loan-verb forms whose keys are the only forms the Woordenlijst lists. Five texts are tightened where a careful reader could object: a verb form of the wrong verb, an over-broad vocative rule, a 't kofschip rule stated before its exception, «романы» for works that include a поэма, and «rabbit» without the species.\n\nSigned-off-by: ValeraZSD <owner@example.test>",
     "committer": {
      "date": "2026-11-24T13:40:01Z"
     }
    }
   },
   {
    "sha": "6f351b72b84059d6721b94a9953e869289f4c11f",
    "parents": [
     {
      "sha": "43c71d07cf13e5cb4d29b7e4063bc8b0057dbf38"
     }
    ],
    "commit": {
     "message": "Name both 't kofschip exceptions up front\n\nSigned-off-by: ValeraZSD <owner@example.test>",
     "committer": {
      "date": "2026-11-24T14:06:16Z"
     }
    }
   },
